```dart
group(
 'name',
 skip: ...,
 () {
   ... body ...
 },
);
``
The original closing was ` });` (group close). With my multi-line form, the closing should be ` },\n );` — but actually ` });` would close `()` and `;` — `group(a, b, () { ... });` — the final `});` closes the callback paren-group: `}` then `)` then `;` — that WORKS syntactically for `group(..., () { ... });` even when args are split across lines! `});` = close callback brace, close group's paren, semicolon. So no closing edit needed. 

